=== HISTORICAL RECORD, and a loss ===

The collection-phase log this file replaces described a 63-entry corpus with
ids BUG-0001..BUG-0063 contiguous, and named the script it ran its checks with:
`check_corpus.py`. That script was never committed, so AMB-35's one substantive
criterion rested on a log referencing something nobody could run. It is now
tests/corpus/check-corpus.py.

Two entries — BUG-0009 and BUG-0063 — were withdrawn between that log and the
corpus's first commit, which already read `entry_count: 61` (912f7ce). No
record of WHY survives, because the log holding it was untracked. Regenerating
this file under AMB-123 did not destroy that reason; it was already outside the
repository. The gap is now ledgered in check-corpus.py's RETIRED table, which
states what is known and explicitly declines to assert what is not.

Figures the old log recorded, carried forward as history rather than as
findings of this run: 63 entries drawn from 78 raw candidates, 15 removed as
duplicates of the same underlying bug with merged URLs retained; 63/63 with an
http(s) source URL; six entries flagged needs-source-recheck (BUG-0009, 0031,
0034, 0035, 0045, 0051), of which AMB-36 later re-fetched and corrected five.

Coverage NOT provided by this run, stated rather than hidden:
  - The corpus file itself (corpus/bugs.yaml) is checked by
    tests/corpus/check-corpus.py as of AMB-123; before that nothing
    validated it at all and its collection-phase log named a script
    (check_corpus.py) that was never committed.
  - Citation spaces ga, ga-excluded, nongoal, req and v2-deferred are
    transcribed from Notion specifications, not resolved against them;
    the gate reports this on every run.
